t(1, 760, """With a worry resembling the worry of the UN Secretary-General, I followed the audacity in one of the mosques of al-Sham against the state's preacher. Audacity against the Friday preacher is audacity against the state .. it has no other meaning .. If every person in any state stood up and did whatever he wished however he wished, we would be facing every day the kind of insolence that happened 1400 years ago on the outskirts of the city of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then developed into the shedding of the blood of Caliph Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), then the shedding of the Ummah's blood .. As for this, it is of that kind; and whoever does not grasp the lessons of history has grasped nothing. The Ummah, by the grace of Allah Almighty, was spared a second edition of Siffin by the swallowing of the army. Those who unleashed their tongues against the Friday preacher in al-Sham are nothing but a plant that sprouted yesterday from a plant that had grown 1400 years ago, at whose hands the Ummah fell and drowned. Al-Sham will be opened as a promise, even if after 100 years; al-Sham will be purified, by Allah's leave, of its turbidity and will become, by Allah's leave, for "its people": the chosen Abdal in righteousness and obedience to Allah Almighty, not for those dragged like sheep toward the follies of the poisoned history that ruined the Ummah, which will be demolished by the might of Allah Almighty, willingly or unwillingly.""")

