t(13, 375, """The return of humans backward is coming again! Those who do not believe it are very pitiable!

The Late Bronze Age (around 1200 BC) ended with one of the greatest civilisational collapses in human history. Within a few decades great civilisations vanished and humanity went back several centuries, into what is known as the "Dark Ages".

Before 1200 BC, the Middle East and the Mediterranean basin lived an integrated, tightly interconnected international order resembling our world today. There was a "first globalisation" order based on:

Interconnected great powers: the New Egyptian Empire, the Hittite Empire (in present-day Turkey), the Mycenaean civilisation (in Greece) and the Kingdom of Babylon.

International trade: bronze was the "oil" of that age (for making weapons and tools). Making bronze required mixing copper (from Cyprus) with tin (from present-day Afghanistan). This was the basis of a complex international trade network vital for survival.

The world did not fall because of one factor, but because of a set of disasters overlapping at the same time (what is called systemic collapse):

Climate change and drought: a long, harsh drought struck the region and lasted for decades. This led to crops withering and great famines, pushing entire peoples to migrate in search of food.

The invasions of the "Sea Peoples": mysterious groups of warriors and migrants appeared across the sea (known historically as the Sea Peoples). They were not just invading armies but whole families moving with their livestock. They attacked the coasts and destroyed the coastal cities one after another.

Internal revolts: because of drought, famine and heavy taxes, trust collapsed between peoples and their rulers (the royal elites), leading to internal revolts and civil wars that ground the cities down from within.

Collapse of supply chains: as soon as wars and drought cut the trade routes, the flow of tin and copper stopped. Armies were unable to make new weapons, and the economy was completely paralysed.

The world fell like dominoes

Total destruction: great cities and giant trading ports such as "Ugarit" in Syria and "Hattusa", the Hittite capital, were burned and destroyed.

The vanishing of empires: the Hittite Empire collapsed completely and faded from history. The Mycenaean kingdoms in Greece disintegrated.

Egypt's withdrawal: ancient Egypt (under Ramesses III) managed to repel the attacks of the Sea Peoples in famous naval and land battles, but came out of the war weak and economically exhausted, and entered a long period of decline.

After the collapse, the region entered centuries of civilisational regression:

Languages and writing systems vanished, because the elite and the scribes had been killed or scattered!

It took centuries for humans to return to writing again.""")

h(14, 300, """The world went backward before! The end of the Bronze Age!""")

t(14, 780, """A report (athar) and a hadith which many Muslims understand as a "certificate of infallibility" from errors and sins, before and after, in the lives of the people they speak of. This is an intellectual and mental naivety that should not exist after Muslims have grasped the details of what preceded the events of the Great Fitnah, and a political intellectual lapse in awareness and method that could not possibly come from the central figure of the end times who appears in that age and that late time!

The report
-----------
"When trade and roads are cut off and fitnahs multiply, seven scholarly men will come out from different horizons, without prior appointment …"

A group of researchers and speakers argued that describing them with the word "scholars" means they are protected from committing errors after they are given power on earth, after the humiliation and weakness they lived in. This is a mistake in inference and an error in grasping what minds necessarily perceive clearly, something people of reason do not differ about! The word "scholars" carries a description of goodness, yes, but it carries no guarantee of the soul remaining good after being given power on earth, no guarantee of the soul's goodness remaining firm until death, and the word "scholars" carries no guarantee of not being affected by power, nor of the soul's impulses not entering conduct and conscience.

The hadith
------------
"Twelve thousand will come out of Aden Abyan, supporting Allah and His Messenger; they are the best of those between me and them."

Goodness is also described here in the hadith, and it is authentic, in the Musnad of Imam Ahmad. But goodness is one thing and infallibility another. Remaining firm on goodness is guaranteed only for someone about whom a text of revelation came confirming his firmness on goodness until his death. A Muslim is always treated with good opinion, and the one whom the Lord of Might purified through revelation to His Prophet ﷺ is given precedence; but a Muslim about whom there is no text of revelation of a good ending is not granted infallibility from sins, errors and perhaps disasters and calamities, even if he began well.

Summary
------------
In the report and the hadith there is a commendation of both parties, and this commendation necessarily means the respect the Ummah owes to both components mentioned in the report and the hadith among the people of that time at the end of days. But those mentioned in the report and the hadith must not be treated, after they are given power on earth and after their psychological state changes from weakness and humiliation to power, leadership and control, as if they were above oversight, above accountability, above scrutiny, follow-up and monitoring; nor be regarded as trustworthy in everything, guided aright in everything, and fit for everything in all their states and at all times. Then the people of that time would think that criticising them is forbidden and that holding them to account is improper and not valid in Shariah, and the people of that time would think that giving them a free hand is a decisive, definite Shariah obligation in the Ummah, and that anything less is an error and among the forbidden things and major sins!""")

h(15, 300, """On understanding the hadiths of commendation: commendation is not infallibility!""")

t(15, 780, """The struggle over rule is a human inevitability with no escape, even at the highest degrees of purity of revolutions in thought, method and goals! Power is the highest degree of human intoxication! Power is the greatest danger threatening the soundness of the human spirit! Power is a fuel in the soul that never stops burning! Power is a burning inevitability that devours itself, and the bet on the purity of the path in it does not always win and certainly does not hold!

And the hadith of the 7 scholars is not a hadith .. it is a report (athar), and people insist on regarding it as a hadith .. And even if it is a report transmitted from a hadith, the people speaking about it took it for a commendation! They took it for a certificate of goodness! A certificate of salvation from the soul's impulses! A report: if authentic, then it is authentic; and if authentic, I have in it a true vision, by Allah's leave, 12 years ago! And another 10 years ago!

The one of which something will be disclosed is the one from 12 years ago, since in goodness and firmness on the path no one is safe from fitnah in them! It is power .. and the struggle for power in East and West has always been one: sometimes it matches exactly between the people of the earth's east and its west, sometimes it is similar, and sometimes it differs only in appearance and tools, but it is always and forever one throughout history, and will remain one, even in the greatest states in goodness and purity!

It does not matter that you start with a sound beginning; what matters is that you stay sound until you leave office! In a vision I saw in 2014, one of them turned into a fingertip!

The truth is that testing the world's experiences deeply makes us understand very well that Trotsky is an inevitable model in the rise of power and in founding it through sincere people, then at the start of the stage of a coup against everyone! Power is a dangerous taste and the desire to taste it is more dangerous, and the idea of making puppets is more and more and more dangerous. The greatest danger in the idea of the "puppet ruler" is that the 7, or half or a quarter of them, think they are choosing a puppet then; that is when the farce happens, and it is a farce almost inevitable with no escape, because we are in an age of corrupted minds!""")

h(15, 2100, """Leon Trotsky: a historical inevitability with no escape! Every revolution has a fuel that devours itself!""")

t(16, 245, """Dozens of reasons that have nothing to do with religion, nor with faith, nor with Jerusalem itself! Rather, among its most important goals was protecting Europe from hundreds of thousands of warlords inside Europe.

Old European social traditions invented the right of primogeniture, whereby the first son (the eldest) in each family inherited everything and the rest of the children inherited nothing. So over time hundreds of thousands of angry rebels arose on the continent, plundering Europe's villages, raiding everything and forming gangs everywhere.

Faced with this disastrous scene, the Pope saw that the solution lay in gathering all these gangs that had drowned Europe in violence that was taking it toward being torn apart, and he gathered them under an ideological banner whose title was: God wills it!

Throughout the history of the Crusades, 9 campaigns set out from the continent under this slogan. The truth is that the world after the six main Crusades that reached the East was never like the world before them .. The Crusades that changed the world astonishingly were 6 campaigns: five reached al-Sham and one lost its way to Constantinople .. 5 wars targeted Jerusalem and a sixth war weakened Constantinople. These 6 military campaigns founded the shape of today's modern world, as the mind of Venice in that age, and with it the Knights Templar, turned to inventing and devising new economic methods, among them a system for transferring money from continent to continent. Those 6 campaigns produced hundreds of results that later affected humanity politically, economically, socially, historically, in science and in invention. One of these Crusades was an almost direct cause of the later conquest of Constantinople, because the Fourth Crusade, instead of heading to Jerusalem, headed to Christian Constantinople; the soldiers of the campaign looted Constantinople and left it weak, worn out and ready to be taken by the Muslims, though that came later, not at the same time.

The Crusades were nothing but wars launched, for their leaders, those who called for them and those who understood the game, for a thousand reasons; yet among the thousand reasons there was not one reason connected to Jerusalem or to the Messiah! As for the soldiers, they had set out precisely for Jerusalem and for the Messiah ..

The Crusades had reaped enormous wealth later used by Europe's kingdoms to fund researchers, thinkers and scholars. Without the Crusades, Europe would not have:
🔴 escaped internal fragmentation
🔴 been able to launch the Renaissance that later made it master of the world!

And perhaps
🔴 the Turks' conquest of Constantinople would have been a little harder

It is hard to list the very many benefits ((Europe)) gained financially, politically, economically, militarily, socially, scientifically and in prosperity from its six main campaigns against the East.

Summary
We have always been, and still are, a garbage dump for ((European political thought)) wrapped in European ideological slogans to stir up the European masses through all ages; we have always been a field of experiments for them. The Knights Templar too had the most distinguished role in making the Europe we see today during the main Crusades, and explaining their role, and the role of Venice in Italy, would take long. But the seventh campaign is coming in northern Syria and it will be the last .. The call to the seventh Crusade at the end of time will be made under the same slogans as the six main campaigns: God wills it; and then Allah's will shall show itself not in words but in the outcome!""")

h(16, 2300, """Had the Crusades not been launched, Europe would have been torn into thousands of pieces!""")

